WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.700
New York City's new job center. The line to get in. All these people hoping to get a job

00:05.700 --> 00:11.200
with the city. About 2,500 people went.

00:11.200 --> 00:16.300
The line was endless. As you can see, it keeps on going and going. All this is looking for

00:16.300 --> 00:23.900
a job with the city. This is insane. It shows you how messed up things are right now in the world.

00:23.900 --> 00:33.700
[Reading a post] "I'll save you the trouble as someone who went on opening day today: they started turning people away after noon. Once I made it a bit further up the line..."

00:33.700 --> 00:41.600
"...I learned they're not currently hiring anyone or accepting resumes. They're only helping people apply on the city jobs website."

00:41.600 --> 00:44.400
This is when they started turning people away.

00:44.400 --> 00:51.500
This is not on any media sites as well. These are the videos I'm seeing online from people recording their experiences.

00:51.500 --> 00:58.900
The Mayor's office did text me about this opening, and I did go, but it was closed that day, and it was warned that it will get crazy on opening day.

00:58.900 --> 01:07.700
But these are all people trying to find a job, particularly with the City of New York.

01:09.500 --> 01:17.600
This is nuts. This shows you how rough it is to find a job in New York. Look how long that line is.
